Tristan Hsiung 501311581 Lab 1

If a better sort function was given, it could be implemented in the 
mySort.c file. This is because mySort already recieves the same parameters
as the betterSort function. The function can be implemented as below.

void mySort(int data[], unsigned int n) {
        betterSort(data, 0, n);
    }
    
It is worth noting that the n does not need to be subtracted by one since
it is taken into account in the main file. This allows mySort to keep 
its signature function while taking advantage of the more efficient 
sorting algorithm provided.
